From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Murray <mark.murray@arm.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Skip AArch64 FPCR test without FP support

The AArch64 test accesses FPCR directly to verify that fesetenv restores
the flush-to-zero bit. When compiling for an architecture with floating
point disabled, Clang rejects the FPCR system-register accesses.

Only build this part of the test when the target has floating-point
support.
---
 test/test-math/test-fenv.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test/test-math/test-fenv.c b/test/test-math/test-fenv.c
index d0eb5538e..78c346250 100644
--- a/test/test-math/test-fenv.c
+++ b/test/test-math/test-fenv.c
@@ -271,7 +271,7 @@ main(void)
     }
 #endif
 
-#ifdef __aarch64__
+#if defined(__aarch64__) && defined(__ARM_FP)
     /* fesetenv restores all of fpcr, including flush-to-zero */
     {
         fenv_t   env;
-- 
2.34.1
